BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - CGCA Prep/Dog About Town (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261025T181500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261025T191500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261025T010005Z
UID:1792952100_Specialty-CGCAPrep/DogAboutTown@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Ready to test your dog's skills in the real world? This class 
 will focus on real-life applications for the behaviors you learned in Adva
 nced Manners class! We'll start off at Lucky Dog for the first week and sp
 end the other 3 weeks of class meeting at various dog-friendly locations. 
 If your dog already has their Canine Good Citizen Title\, this class will 
 also prepare you for the Community Canine\, or CGCA\, test. See descriptio
 n below.\nCommunity Canine (CGCA) is the advanced level of AKC’s Canine 
 Good Citizen (CGC) program. Like the CGC\, dogs must pass a 10-step test o
 f skills to earn their CGCA award. The test focuses on real-world scenario
 s and testing your dog's skills in a more natural setting\, such as in a s
 tore or at the park.
END:VEVENT
